[{"code":"list_may_be_shared","severity":"error","span":{"file":"Main.beni","start":{"line":14,"col":17},"end":{"line":15,"col":97}},"title":"LIST MAY BE SHARED","message":"`Dict.foldr` changes `Main.shared#Dict.0#Node.2` in place, and the checker\ncannot show that nothing else still holds the list.\n\n14|                Dict.foldr (Dict.fromList [ ( 1, 1 ), ( 2, 2 ) ]) shared λ_ x acc →\n                   ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ the list is changed in place here\n\n6|shared = Dict.insert Dict.empty 1 [ 0 ]\n  ^^^^^^ the top-level list is defined here\n\nCopy the list with `List.copy` before it is changed, so the change cannot reach\nanything else that holds it.\n\nThis is a limit of the checker, not proof of sharing: Main.shared is a top-level\nvalue; the callee writes it only through an approximate step."},{"code":"list_may_be_shared","severity":"error","span":{"file":"Main.beni","start":{"line":15,"col":21},"end":{"line":15,"col":97}},"title":"LIST MAY BE SHARED","message":"`Dict.update` changes `acc#Dict.0#Node.2` in place, and the checker cannot show\nthat nothing else still holds the list.\n\n15|                    Dict.update acc 1 λold → Just (List.append (Maybe.withDefault old []) [ x ])\n                       ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ the list is changed in place here\n\nCopy the list with `List.copy` before it is changed, so the change cannot reach\nanything else that holds it.\n\nThis is a limit of the checker, not proof of sharing: it needs what Dict.foldr\nsupplies it not to share, and it may."}]
